================================================================================
Intelligence → Analytics: show the loading spinner immediately on section open
================================================================================

Context:
Opening /intelligence/?section=analytics left the Analytics pane empty for
seconds before the spinner appeared. analyticsLoadTypes() first awaited the
graph probe (/dtwin/sync/stats: 2.3-3.3 s on the dev server, p90 7.1 s in the
logs) and only then called analyticsLoadLatest(), which is where the spinner
was shown. /dtwin/metrics/latest and /dtwin/metrics/series also read the
registry synchronously on the event loop.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/query/js/query-analytics.js
   - analyticsLoadTypes() shows the "Loading the last analysis…" spinner
     right away and starts the /dtwin/metrics/latest fetch in parallel with
     the graph probe.
   - analyticsResume(prefetched) / analyticsLoadLatest(prefetched) reuse
     that in-flight promise; the stored result is still rendered only after
     the _graphMissing gate (stale-result contract unchanged). The missing
     graph path now hides the spinner.
   - New helpers _showLoadingLatestSpinner / _hideLoadingLatestSpinner
     (default compute message kept in data-default-msg and restored) and
     _fetchLatestMetrics.
2. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   - GET /dtwin/metrics/latest and /dtwin/metrics/series read the stored
     metrics through run_blocking.
3. tests/units/front/test_analytics_stale_result_gate.py
   - Spinner shown before the probe, latest prefetched during the probe,
     missing-graph path hides the spinner.

