================================================================================
Certified graph: two-stage design (SPEC + PLAN, no code change)
================================================================================

Context:
Design study for splitting the knowledge graph into a no-copy live graph
(Delta, used to navigate, enrich, curate and certify) and a certified graph
built by a second build into Lakebase, Lakehouse (materialized Delta) or
Neo4j, which is the only graph served to MCP and the external API, and only
for PUBLISHED versions. Decisions recorded: non-certified patterns are
forbidden (whitelist), inferences are re-derived on the cleaned base, a
successful certified build is required to publish, and MCP serves only
PUBLISHED versions.

Changes:
1. .planning/certified-graph/SPEC.md
   - Purpose, decisions D1-D4, live graph (live build, _enriched with
     provenance, curation ledger, pattern whitelist), certified build
     phases (base, whitelist, re-derivation, stage, gates, load through the
     existing pipelines), naming, atomicity, lifecycle, serving, migration,
     success criteria, risks.
2. .planning/certified-graph/PLAN.md
   - Code smells and Fowler refactorings, phases P1 (two stages,
     behaviour-equivalent) to P4 (operations), open points, verification.

