================================================================================
Settings → UI: reorganised and explained branding / theme page
================================================================================

Context:
The UI settings page stacked two cards, repeated the "Admin only" badge three
times, split every colour into separate "picker" and "Hex value" columns and
gave little explanation of what each colour drives (Aurora in particular).
The live preview was also misleading: `.ui-branding-preview-btn` repainted
both preview buttons with Primary, while real Create / Share buttons use
their own colours.

Changes:
1. src/front/templates/settings.html (#ui-section)
   - One card under the section header (Section Body Surface rule), with a
     single admin note explaining Save / Discard changes / Default and that
     the default entity icon is saved immediately.
   - Branding block: title and default entity icon side by side, logo row
     with the Reset icon button next to the file input (stacked on small
     screens); help texts say where each item appears.
   - Theme block: the four colours (Primary, Aurora, Create button, Share
     button) each show picker + hex on one line and a help text describing
     what they drive; a sticky "Live preview" panel (active item with the
     Primary → Aurora bar, hovered row, Create / Share buttons, focused
     field) and the derived palette with a usage caption per swatch.
   - Hex inputs get accessible names; every existing id, aria-describedby
     association and JS hook is unchanged.
2. src/front/static/global/css/config.css
   - Removed the .ui-branding-preview-btn override so the preview shows the
